# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the keys you want for local development.
# Every source below is optional. Without a key that source is skipped, and the
# app still works from the no-key sources (Eventbrite UK and the built-in local
# guide). On Render, set these in the dashboard instead.

# Ticketmaster Discovery API. Free key: https://developer.ticketmaster.com/
# VenTrack queries it with countryCode=GB, so it only ever returns UK events.
# Covers concerts, theatre, comedy and arena sport.
TM_API_KEY=

# Skiddle. Free key: https://www.skiddle.com/api/
# A UK-only listings service: gigs, club nights, festivals, comedy and food
# events, with coordinates and prices in pounds on every result. The single
# most useful key to set for this market.
SKIDDLE_API_KEY=

# TheSportsDB. Free key: https://www.thesportsdb.com/api.php
# Upcoming fixtures for the English leagues and the Scottish Premiership.
# Football is the biggest category the ticketing sources miss, because most
# clubs sell through their own box office.
THESPORTSDB_KEY=

# PredictHQ. Free key: sign up at https://control.predicthq.com/ then generate
# an access token under Access Tokens. Despite the _KEY suffix (kept for
# consistency with the three above) it is sent as a Bearer token, not a query
# parameter, so nothing else about how you use it changes.
# An events intelligence feed: concerts, festivals, performing arts, expos,
# community listings and sport, worldwide, queried here with country=GB. It
# carries no ticket link and no image, so the app falls back to the category
# mark for those, but it is the one source that sometimes gives a real
# description, which is used in place of the generic fallback text.
PREDICTHQ_API_KEY=

# OpenAI. Not free like the four above: this is a paid API key, and every page
# scanned costs a small real amount against it. Powers sources/localscan.js,
# which reads the community pages listed in sources/localscan-seeds.js and
# has an LLM pull out real events that never reach a ticketing platform. No
# key means the source returns nothing, exactly like every source above; a
# key with no seed pages listed also returns nothing, since the seed list is
# what actually costs money. See the "A fifth key" and "Adding a page to
# watch" sections in DEPLOY.md before setting this one.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional: comma-separated region ids to keep warm on boot and on the refresh
# timer. Defaults to london,manchester,birmingham,glasgow. Ids come from
# sources/regions.js (also listed by GET /api/status).
# WARM_REGIONS=london,manchester,birmingham,glasgow

# Optional: the App Store listing the landing page's button links to. Leave it
# unset and the page says "Coming soon to the App Store" as plain text rather
# than a dead button, which is what you want before launch.
# APP_STORE_URL=https://apps.apple.com/gb/app/ventrack/id0000000000

# Optional: serve the web app at /app for local development. Never set this in
# production. The web app is the same product as the paid iOS app, so serving
# it publicly gives the whole thing away. See README.md.
# SERVE_WEB_APP=1

# Keep-alive. Nothing to set: on Render the service finds its own public URL
# from RENDER_EXTERNAL_URL and pings /healthz every 10 minutes so a free
# instance never hits the ~15 minute idle timeout. It is inert locally, since
# that variable only exists on Render. Read keepalive.js before relying on it:
# it prevents a sleep, it cannot end one. Set KEEPALIVE=off after moving to a
# paid plan, where the instance never sleeps and the ping is just noise.
# KEEPALIVE=off
# KEEPALIVE_INTERVAL_MS=600000
# KEEPALIVE_URL=https://pulse-uk-api.onrender.com/healthz
